PN,36602
SC,0002
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F366A1786382335
OL,3,CLittler warns he can still get better
OL,4,Cafter retaining World Matchplay title
OL,6,FThe 19-year-old, from Warrington,
OL,7,FCheshire, also broke his own
OL,8,Fcompetition record for 180s as he hit
OL,9,F12 in the final to reach 66 for the
OL,10,Fweek.
OL,12,FThe win keeps Littler on course for a
OL,13,Fclean sweep of trophies in 2026 having
OL,14,Falready won the World Championship, UK
OL,15,FOpen, Premier League and the Masters.
OL,17,FBut while the 19-year-old said this
OL,18,Fwas the best version of himself to
OL,19,Fdate, there is still plenty more to
OL,20,Fcome.
OL,1,W~k4j5 hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}      G2/7
OL,2,W/*%+.-' "-$/*%+.!+,*%/*%/*-'R(,,,,,,,,,
